{
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Inter-Graph Edge Semantics Q&A",
    "kind": "investigation",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "preferredViewer": "https://twilite.zone"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "inter-graph-edge-semantics-declaration",
      "type": "declaration",
      "label": "Inter-Graph Edge Semantics",
      "position": {
        "x": -520,
        "y": -440
      },
      "width": 400,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "inter-graph-edge-semantics",
          "nodeId": "inter-graph-edge-semantics",
          "name": "Inter-Graph Edge Semantics",
          "version": "0.1.0",
          "description": "A provisional Q&A investigation into edge identity, bridge participation, and workspace rendering across graph documents and semantic node boundaries."
        },
        "intent": {
          "kind": "investigation",
          "scope": "local"
        },
        "document": {
          "url": "github://twilite-zone/public/tasks/inter-graph-edge-semantics/root.node"
        },
        "declaration": {
          "kind": "investigation",
          "targetMode": "artifact",
          "defaultSurfaceId": "",
          "surfaces": []
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "What feels off?",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -440
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 330,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#241d32",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# What feels off?\n\nWe are treating several workspace lines as if they were interchangeable:\n\n- a Portal following a Port\n- an export/import Bridge pair\n- an authored edge crossing a graph-document seam\n- an edge between two rendered semantic nodes\n- a derived workspace route\n\nThey may look similar, but they do not necessarily have the same identity or authority."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-visible-line",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q1 · Is every workspace line an edge?",
      "position": {
        "x": -900,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nIs every line drawn between node regions a graph edge?\n\n## Provisional answer\n\nNo. A Portal binding can visualize traversal or shared presentation without asserting a semantic relationship. Workspace geometry is a projection and cannot create an edge merely by being drawn."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-bridge",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q2 · Is a Bridge an edge?",
      "position": {
        "x": -440,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nDoes a Bridge own an edge, or does it expose/consume a place where an edge may cross?\n\n## Working hypothesis\n\nA Bridge is a graph-local boundary node. A matched export/import pair may be evidence that one authored relationship crosses the seam. An unmatched export is a capability, not yet an edge."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-owner",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q3 · Who owns edge type?",
      "position": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nWhere does semantic edge-class identity belong?\n\n## Candidates\n\n1. The logical edge.\n2. The Bridge pair.\n3. Each graph-local edge segment.\n4. The workspace projection.\n\nThe answer must survive closing either graph and must not depend on the current layout."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-one-or-two",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q4 · One edge or two?",
      "position": {
        "x": 480,
        "y": 20
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nWhen a relationship crosses graph documents, is it one logical edge with two stored projections, or two edges joined by Bridges?\n\n## Test\n\nCan it have one label, one class, one deletion operation, and one stable identity while each document remains independently saveable?"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-same-node",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q5 · Same node, different graphs",
      "position": {
        "x": -900,
        "y": 360
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nIf two graph documents declare the same semantic `nodeId`, is an edge across their document seam inter-node at all?\n\n## Provisional answer\n\nIt may be an internal relationship within one rendered node. The graph seam still matters for persistence, but the workspace should not invent a semantic boundary that the node model does not contain."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-different-node",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q6 · Different semantic nodes",
      "position": {
        "x": -440,
        "y": 360
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nWhat permits an edge between different rendered nodes?\n\n## Provisional answer\n\nThere must be real endpoint instances in both owning graphs and an authored relationship operation. Merely opening two graphs, following a Portal, or matching adjacency is insufficient."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-portal",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q7 · Do Portals carry edge classes?",
      "position": {
        "x": 20,
        "y": 360
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nShould a Portal route inherit an edge class?\n\n## Provisional answer\n\nProbably not. A Portal identifies a destination Port and supports traversal. If following it also instantiates a relationship, that newly authored edge may have a class; the Portal itself remains navigational."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "q-bridge-class",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Q8 · How does a Bridge constrain type?",
      "position": {
        "x": 480,
        "y": 360
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#172033",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Question\n\nWhat does an export Bridge say about edge type?\n\n## Candidate rule\n\nA Bridge can expose an allowed or required relationship capability. The import side must accept it. This constrains creation, but does not automatically make the Bridge the owner of the resulting edge class."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "candidate",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Candidate synthesis — not yet law",
      "position": {
        "x": -620,
        "y": 720
      },
      "width": 650,
      "height": 430,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#18302b",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Candidate synthesis\n\n1. **An edge exists only when an authored relationship exists.**\n2. **The relationship owns its semantic edge-class identity.**\n3. **Bridge nodes are persistent graph-local endpoints at document boundaries.**\n4. **A matched Bridge pair lets one relationship be reconstructed across documents.**\n5. **The workspace route is derived from that relationship and its open endpoint graphs.**\n6. **Portal/shared-surface routes remain a separate visual vocabulary.**\n7. **Same-node multi-graph expansion may cross a persistence seam without crossing a semantic node boundary.**\n\nThis is a hypothesis to test against current data, editing gestures, deletion, save isolation, and collapsed graphs."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "counterexample",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Counterexample hunt",
      "position": {
        "x": 80,
        "y": 720
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 430,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#38231d",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Try to break the synthesis\n\n- Can two edge instances of different classes use the same Bridge?\n- Can one export be consumed more than once?\n- Does an import Bridge exist before its edge?\n- What remains visible when one endpoint graph is closed?\n- Does same-node expansion require Bridges at all?\n- Which document owns label and route-pin edits?\n- Can an edge class require a particular Port type?\n- What happens when the two stored halves disagree?"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "plan",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Investigation plan",
      "position": {
        "x": -620,
        "y": 1200
      },
      "width": 650,
      "height": 430,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#1d2940",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# Plan\n\n1. Inventory actual persisted shapes for local edges, inter-graph `edgeReferences`, export/import Bridges, and Portal bindings.\n2. Build four tiny fixtures: Portal-only, unmatched Bridge, matched Bridge without edge, and typed authored edge across two documents.\n3. Write the expected create, open, close, save, reopen, change-class, and delete behavior for each.\n4. Decide the canonical owner of `logicalEdgeId` and edge-class identity only after comparing those fixtures.\n5. Implement one resolver that produces a renderable logical relationship.\n6. Let local canvas and workspace renderers consume that same result.\n7. Keep compatibility readers for current Bridge `relationship.edgeClass*` data until migration is deliberate."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "acceptance",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Decision gate",
      "position": {
        "x": 80,
        "y": 1200
      },
      "width": 520,
      "height": 430,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "style": {
        "background": "#2d2440",
        "color": "#eef4ff",
        "borderColor": "#52627d",
        "borderWidth": 1,
        "borderStyle": "solid",
        "borderRadius": 16
      },
      "data": {
        "markdown": "# We are ready to implement when…\n\n- We can say whether matched Bridges without an authored edge draw anything.\n- We can distinguish navigation lines from relationship edges without color alone.\n- One edge-class change has an unambiguous persistence owner.\n- Closing a graph does not destroy or silently reclassify the relationship.\n- Same-node document seams and different-node boundaries behave intentionally.\n- Both graph-local and workspace-scale renderers receive the same semantic edge contract."
      }
    }
  ],
